    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PECO_0007359 -->

    <Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PECO_0007359">
        <rdfs:label>plant experimental condition</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
        <oboInOwl:id>PECO:0007359</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>plant treatment (related)</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <ns3:IAO_0000115>A plant exposure (PECO:0001001) and/or study condition (PECO:0007231) applied to a whole plant (PO:0000003), a plant structure (PO:00090119), and/or a plant population.</ns3:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>The Plant Experimental Condition Ontology describes the treatments and/or study conditions used in plant biology experiments. The subjects of the studies may also include in vitro plant structures (PO:0000004). The broadest classes are the plant study conditions (PECO:0007231), where the terms describe the type of growth facility used in an experiment. Each study type such as field study (PECO:0007256), growth chamber study (PECO:0007269), greenhouse study (PECO:0007248), or laboratory study (PECO:0007255) will also involve different growing conditions, and may also include specific biotic (PECO:0007357) and/or abiotic (PECO:0007191) plant treatments. A plant exposure (PECO:0001001) may be a component of a plant experimental condition (PECO:0007359), and the plant study condition (PECO:0007231).</rdfs:comment>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>EO:0007359</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>PECO_GIT:4</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>plant_experimental_conditions_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
    </Class>
</rdf:RDF>



